<header><p class="enc-kicker">Historical factor</p><h1 class="enc-title">Diplomacy and marriage alliances</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Diplomacy and marriage alliances describes the use of treaties, gifts and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diplomatic-marriage">dynastic marriages</a> to win allies, legitimise rule and expand influence without war. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gupta-empire">Gupta Empire</a> benefited from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chandragupta-i">Chandragupta I</a>'s marriage into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/licchavi">Licchavi</a> clan, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mitanni">Mitanni Empire</a> sent royal princesses to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonian-empire">Macedonian Empire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a> both used alliances to secure their rise.</p></div>
